[COMMENTS]
STATION,Crump profile weir gauging a rural, Chalk catchment with some Boulder Clay and terrace deposits and with some artificial influences, all but the very highest flows are contained. GENERAL: Crump profile weir 4m wide, situated approx. 20m u/s of new road bridge. STATION HYDROMETRY: The POR maximum flow is believed to have been in Sept 1968, estimated as 15.1 cumecs by the EA but likely to have been extrapolated. FLOW RECORD: Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2020 (WINFAP Files v9). FLOW REGIME: Some groundwater abstraction for PWS, also industrial/agricultural abstraction. Runoff increased by effluent returns.
CATCHMENT,A rural Chalk catchment with Boulder Clay cover in upper (S) part of catchment. Some river terrace deposits in N. Mixed agricultural land use.
Qmed Suitability,Although not gauged to within 30% of QMED, theoretical rating expected to perform well to QMED.
Pooling Suitability,Few high flow gaugings. Rating can not be validated beyond QMED.
[END]
